# Button content alignment

Layout is derived automatically from which icon slots are filled — do not add a `centered` prop or manual flex overrides at call sites.

Shared logic lives in `src/components/buttonContentLayout.ts`.

## Rules

| Icons | Alignment |
|-------|-----------|
| Leading only | Centre icon + label as a group |
| Trailing only | Label left, icon right (`space-between`) |
| Leading + trailing | Leading icon + label left as a cluster; trailing icon right |
| No icons | Centre label |

## Usage

```tsx
// Centre group — leading icon only
<PrimaryButton label="add set" leadingIcon="plus" trailingIcon="none" />

// Label left, arrow right — onboarding CTA
<PrimaryButton label="next" trailingIcon="arrow" />

// Do not pass centered or flex:1 on the label
```

When adding a new button variant, extend `getButtonContentLayout` rather than inlining alignment styles.
